/*! \page page_logger AnCH logging library documentation
 *
 * \tableofcontents
 *
 * \section log_intro_seq Introduction
 *
 * AnCH logging library provides configurable loggers which write messages through writers (console,
 * files with rotation), with a map diagnostic context.
 *
 * \section log_prereq_sec Prerequisites
 *
 * - anch-conf: logging configuration is read in the \c anch::log section of the application configuration
 * - anch-date: high precision dates in messages
 * - anch-utils: singletons
 *
 * \section log_install_sec Installation
 *
 * CMake target \c anch::log:
 * \code{.cmake}
find_package(Anch REQUIRED)
target_link_libraries(my-app PRIVATE anch::log)
\endcode
 * See \ref install_sec "installation".
 *
 * \section log_concept_sec Usage
 *
 * Loggers are retrieved with \ref anch::log::LoggerFactory::getLogger "LoggerFactory::getLogger" once the
 * configuration has been loaded. Logger names are hierarchical (\c org::myapp::Main ): the most specific
 * configured logger applies (\c org::myapp , then \c org , then the default logger).\n
 * \n
 * Messages are logged with level methods (\c trace , \c debug , \c info , \c warn , \c error , \c fatal ),
 * which concatenate their arguments, or with stream injection (\c log/stream.hpp ):
 * - levels are types in \ref anch::log::lvl namespace: <tt>LOG << anch::log::lvl::debug << "value=" << value;</tt>
 * - the message is written at the end of the expression ;
 *
 * With both APIs, messages in levels lower than \c ANCH_LOG_MIN_LEVEL CMake option (\c TRACE by default) are removed at
 * compile time. Arguments are always evaluated, even when the level is disabled. Logging never throws.
 *
 * \subsection log_concept_conf_sec Configuration
 *
 * - \c anch::log.thread-safe : writers are protected against concurrent access (default \c true ).
 * - \c anch::log.low-priority : writers write messages in a dedicated thread (default \c false ).
 * - \c [anch::log.writer.\<name\>] : writer declaration:
 *   - \c module : \c console or \c file ;
 *   - \c pattern : message pattern: \c $c logger name, \c $p level, \c $m message, \c $t thread identifier,
 *     \c $d{strftime format} date, \c $D{anch-date format} high precision date, \c $C{key} MDC value ;
 *   - \c path , \c max-size (with \c K , \c M , \c G or \c T unit) and \c max-rotate-files for file writers ;
 *   - \c thread-safe and \c low-priority override the global values.
 * - \c [anch::log.logger] : default logger ; \c [anch::log.logger.\<name\>] : logger for a name prefix:
 *   - \c writers : comma separated writer names ;
 *   - \c level : \c trace , \c debug , \c info , \c warn , \c error or \c fatal .
 *
 * Without \c anch::log section, messages are written on the console.
 *
 * \section log_example_sec Example
 *
 * \c application.ini :
 * \code{.ini}
[anch::log.writer.console]
module=console
pattern=$d{%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S} - $c: $p - $m

[anch::log.writer.file]
module=file
path=./application.log
pattern=$d{%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S} [$t] $p $c - $m
max-size=10M
max-rotate-files=5

[anch::log.logger]
writers=console
level=info

[anch::log.logger.org::myapp]
writers=console,file
level=debug
\endcode
 *
 * \code{.cpp}
#include "conf/configuration.hpp"
#include "log/loggerFactory.hpp"
#include "log/stream.hpp"

int
main() {
  anch::conf::Configuration::loader().name("application").load(); // application.ini (anch::log section)
  const anch::log::Logger& LOG = anch::log::LoggerFactory::getLogger("org::myapp::Main");

  LOG.info("Application started with ", 3, " workers");               // variadic API
  LOG << anch::log::lvl::debug << "value=" << 42 << ", ratio=" << 0.5; // stream API
  return 0;
}
\endcode
 *
 * Console output:
 * \code{.txt}
2026-11-12 21:35:07 - org::myapp::Main: INFO - Application started with 3 workers
2026-11-12 21:35:07 - org::myapp::Main: DEBUG - value=42, ratio=0.5
\endcode
 */
